      "q": 0.0178407399671272,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 3,
      "text": "Step 3: Substitute back to get \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = 143k + 10 \\]\nNow, we need \\( x \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\):\n\\[ 143k + 10 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\]\nSince \\( 143 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7} \\), we have:\n\\[ 6k + 10 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ 6k \\equiv -5 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ 6k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} \\] (since \\(-5 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}\\))",
      "z": -4.008268870194718
    },
