      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 4,
      "text": "Step 4: To solve for \\( k \\), we need the multiplicative inverse of 6 modulo 7. The inverse of 6 modulo 7 is 6, because \\( 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7} \\). So:\n\\[ k \\equiv 2 \\times 6 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ k \\equiv 12 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ k \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\]\nThus, \\( k = 7m + 5 \\) for some integer \\( m \\).",
      "z": -1.6380446969787286
